  (these are 12-speed cores; appending a single parked w gives the 13-set.)
  {1..9} u {14,28,42}                     : meas(G_C)=       1207/8820=0.13684807 r=22 widest=0.017007 prim=True
  {1..6} u 6 coord {14k}                  : meas(G_C)=        611/2940=0.20782313 r=74 widest=0.005952 prim=True
  {1..4} u 8 coord {14k}                  : meas(G_C)=      3427/20580=0.16652089 r=168 widest=0.003189 prim=True
  {1..3} u 9 coord {14k}                  : meas(G_C)=    15499/123480=0.12551830 r=192 widest=0.002268 prim=True
  {1,2} u 10 coord {14k}                  : meas(G_C)=    13387/123480=0.10841432 r=220 widest=0.001531 prim=True
  {1..9} u {98,112,126}(big AP)           : meas(G_C)=      4013/35280=0.11374717 r=46 widest=0.006641 prim=True
  {1..6} u 6 coord big {14*20k}           : meas(G_C)=        256/1225=0.20897959 r=1536 widest=0.000298 prim=True
  {1..4} u 8 coord 7-coprime 14p          : meas(G_C)=892051238707/5194516694367=0.17172940 r=436 widest=0.001655 prim=True

  MIN meas(G_C) over these coordinated 12-cores: 13387/123480=0.10841432  ({1,2} u 10 coord {14k})
  compare extremal single-drop 7/858=0.00815851.
  Is the coordinated min BELOW 7/858? False
  KEY: if a primitive 12-core has meas(G_C) < 7/858, then 7/858 is NOT the universal
  floor and OPEN-Q-108's conjectured constant is WRONG (the reduction would need a
  smaller, possibly zero, uniform bound).

